{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LLM-Review remediation for Gerrit change 1386 (patchset 2 pushed).\n\nBLOCKING FINDING (the only one): bugfix-size-attestation — the change touches 156 non-test lines (>150 floor) on bug 1dbe, but the bug had NO certified plan-review attestation (verdict: unsigned). This is a deterministic coverage gate, not a code defect: an oversized bug fix must carry a valid plan-review op-cert.\n\nREMEDIATION: ran 'rebar review-plan 1dbe' (REBAR_GATE_REF=origin/main, Bedrock). Verdict PASS, 0 blocking, 2 minor advisories (P6 AC-quality, P9 no file_impact). Signed the attestation via 'rebar sign-review 1dbe' (no-LLM re-sign of the PASS sidecar). It now classifies as 'certified' via bugfix_size_gate.classify_plan_review_attestation, so the gate buckets it 'accepted' (coverage note, not a block). Op-cert signed by env ade0f2ef (pinned in trusted_environments.yaml, key matches .opcert-key.pub); SIGNATURE event auto-pushed to origin/tickets at log position after the era anchor, so the review bot verifies it cross-host.\n\nNO code change was needed — the finding was purely the missing attestation. Amended the existing commit (--amend --no-edit, Change-Id/rebar-ticket/DCO preserved) to mint patchset 2 (f1c064aec3) and re-pushed for the bot to re-review. Left ticket in_progress; not submitting/closing (still needs Verified +1 + LLM-Review +1)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785871828753482001,"uuid":"2a97e754-748a-4a8b-a5fc-8c2026a16dfd"}